Profile-hook verification keyring
=================================

profile-keyring.gpg contains the historical TurnKey release public certificate:
694CFF26795A29BAE07B4EB585C25E95A16EB94D
Turnkey Linux Release Key <release@turnkeylinux.com>

Provenance: turnkeylinux/common commit 4e6036c4f8b0ea630658e88afb77231fbf7184bd
parent, overlays/turnkey.d/apt/etc/apt/trusted.gpg.d/turnkey.gpg,
Git blob adf0eab081b2f9c8557ca1694637c6d6bd5ce06e.
SHA256: d7f0b51c3a1fb13ea4e3553b2e09b5b5defa0770466516a68047ab337b4df59c

This certificate authenticates existing signed profile hooks. The certificate
expired on 2023-08-12. Historical signatures remain verifiable using gpgv,
preserving TKLBAM's established signature-verification behavior. This package
does not renew the certificate or re-sign profiles.

The keyring is scoped to profile hooks. APT repository trust and administrator
GPG configuration are managed separately. Missing or invalid profile-hook
signatures stop the operation so required application data cannot be silently
omitted. Reinstall the packaged keyring or restore the authentic profile before
retrying such a failure.
